Vitest suite collection: `describe`/`suite` factories execute during the collection phase regardless of skip mode — this is required for nested test discovery and matches Jest's documented semantics ("describe blocks... run before any tests run"). Vitest is Jest-compatible here. Children of a skipped suite are reported as skipped, which is only possible if the factory ran and registered them. This is consistent with Vitest's own `@vitest/runner` implementation where `createSuiteCollector`'s `collect` runs `await factory(api)` unconditionally and the mode only marks tasks.

